WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.240
What if Zoro killed every pirate he came across&nbsp;
to buy himself a place amongst the celestial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:14.200
dragons? What if Franky used his blueprints to&nbsp;
turn himself into the ancient weapon Pluton?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:20.080
And what if Luffy was the one who stabbed Ace&nbsp;
in the back to become one of the Warlords? In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.400
other words: What would it look like if&nbsp;
the straw hat pirates were truly evil?

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:31.600
Believe it or not, Jinbei was first introduced&nbsp;
all the way back in chapter 69 (nice),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.680
by Zoro’s bounty hunter friends when&nbsp;
they talked about the seven warlords..&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.440
According to their highly inaccurate&nbsp;
silhouettes, these monstrous pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.040
were feared throughout the Grand Line. And&nbsp;
just a few chapters later, Dracule Mihawk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.960
confirmed their power when he cut a massive&nbsp;
ship in half and then nearly cut Zoro in half.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.480
Of course, when we’re finally introduced to&nbsp;
Jinbei, we find out he’s actually just a big,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.400
cuddly Teddy…Shark…Guy…but what would it have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.400
taken for this fearsome fishman&nbsp;
to have turned to the dark side?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:14.120
Well, not much actually. In fact,&nbsp;
Arlong shared a backstory with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:20.280
Jinbei and just look at how he turned out.&nbsp;
After their mentor, Fisher Tiger’s, death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.600
Arlong cursed humans and sought violent revenge&nbsp;
for all the discrimination that the Fishmen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:32.080
faced. Jinbei walked a difficult, but noble&nbsp;
path, in honoring Fisher Tiger’s legacy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.840
deciding to become a Warlord for the greater&nbsp;
good of Fishman Island’s future. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:43.720
Jinbei could have taken the easier way out just&nbsp;
like Arlong. He wouldn’t just want peace for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:51.320
Fishman Island - he’d make Fishman Island a world&nbsp;
power in his conquest for revenge against humans.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:58.200
Jinbei and Arlong could have sailed together as&nbsp;
Co-Captains of the New Sun Pirates, “shining a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.680
light” on the misdeeds of humans throughout the&nbsp;
Grand Line and generally terrorizing the globe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:10.360
together. Using Fishman Karate, Jinbei would cut&nbsp;
down ships, leaving marine soldiers and civilians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:15.400
alike to drown in the dreadful waters of the&nbsp;
world’s most dangerous ocean. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:21.920
this would have caused the World Government to&nbsp;
pass judgment on Fishman Island and after a hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.040
fought battle against the admirals, Arlong and&nbsp;
Jinbei both would have ended up in Impel Down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:34.160
This time, when Luffy finds Jinbei in Level 6 of&nbsp;
Impel Down, he’d actually deserve to be locked up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.640
there. If the humans of the One Piece world would&nbsp;
treat him like a monster, then he’d act like one.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:47.120
The same goes for another monstrous member of&nbsp;
the Straw Hat Crew: Chopper. As a reindeer who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.840
ate the human-human fruit, Chopper was shunned&nbsp;
by the rest of the reindeer in his herd for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.880
being different from everyone else. However,&nbsp;
even though he developed human intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:03.040
the villagers of Drum Island feared him as a&nbsp;
beast. He finally found hope, though, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.800
form of his mentor Dr. Hiruluk who helped&nbsp;
him find his dream of becoming a doctor.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.840
However, once Dr. Hiruluk died, Chopper&nbsp;
was devastated. Not only that, but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.720
felt largely responsible for his mentor’s&nbsp;
death, having given him a poisonous mushroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.480
thinking it would heal his disease.&nbsp;
Imagine if Dr. Kureha had refused Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.160
Hiruluk’s request to take in Chopper&nbsp;
and teach him medicine - or worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:34.640
if Wapol’s army had successfully found and&nbsp;
executed her like he did with the other doctors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.280
who wouldn’t join his private medical team. Man,&nbsp;
thinking about the Drum Island arc, it really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:45.400
might be the only country that has even more&nbsp;
restrictive healthcare than the United States.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.520
In this Dark Timeline, Chopper would&nbsp;
be left to fend for himself in the cold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:59.240
winter wilderness of Drum Island. Residents&nbsp;
of the island’s villages would spread rumors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:05.040
of a beast wandering the snows at night.&nbsp;
They’d warn against going out after dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.000
for the monster would come into the&nbsp;
villages to scavenge for food or supplies.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.480
And what would those supplies be for?&nbsp;
Well, just because Dr. Hiruluk died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:20.400
it doesn’t mean Chopper would lose his&nbsp;
intelligence and curiosity. He’d still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.400
be experimenting with chemistry, but this&nbsp;
time wouldn’t just become knowledgeable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:30.360
in medicine - he’d learn how to manipulate&nbsp;
poisons and other dangerous substances. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.160
would also not follow the same code of ethics&nbsp;
when practicing medicine and would be fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:42.440
willing to experiment on living subjects in order&nbsp;
to develop medicines. When he saw Caesar Clown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:47.040
experimenting on children at Punk Hazard,&nbsp;
he would simply say “hell yeah, brother.”

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:52.000
He would also still use science to experiment&nbsp;
on his own devil fruit transformations using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.680
the rumble balls, which would allow Chopper&nbsp;
to become a true beast by accessing Monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:04.600
Point. Using this power, he’d reduce Wapol’s&nbsp;
castle to rubble and become the de facto ruler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:09.800
of the island. In fact, Oda hints that this&nbsp;
is what would happen to Chopper in a darker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:15.760
timeline. In the SBS sections of the manga&nbsp;
volumes, he’s drawn alternate futures for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:22.280
most of the Straw Hats - and Chopper’s shows&nbsp;
him as a grotesque beast demanding sacrifices.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:27.200
When Luffy and his Evil Crew finally showed&nbsp;
up, they’d think a beast like Evil Chopper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.240
would fit right in on their crew of&nbsp;
monsters - and Chopper would take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:37.080
opportunity to find more knowledge, poisons,&nbsp;
and sacrifices all across the Grand Line.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:43.720
Also joining the Evil Straw Hats on a quest&nbsp;
for knowledge would be the Devil Child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:48.560
Nico Robin. After defeating the Warlord Sir&nbsp;
Crocodile and claiming the Kingdom of Alabasta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:56.080
as his own territory, Luffy would recruit Robin to&nbsp;
his side. Miss All-Sunday had proven herself to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:02.680
a capable and cunning fighter, had saved Luffy’s&nbsp;
life in the hopes he would defeat her employer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:08.160
and came with the added bonus of knowing&nbsp;
how to read the poneglyphs, which were said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:13.080
to reveal the secrets of the Ancient Weapons -&nbsp;
knowledge that could turn the world upside down.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:22.080
Nico Robin had spent her life on the run from the&nbsp;
government, always sticking to the side of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:28.520
strong in order to save herself. When a rising&nbsp;
star showed the potential to become the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:35.320
pirate king, it would be natural for this lifelong&nbsp;
criminal to join his crew. In this timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:42.120
we’d sadly never see the kinder, gentler Robin&nbsp;
that opened up to the Straw Hats. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:47.320
she would silently follow along with the crew&nbsp;
in order to meet her own goal of uncovering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:52.400
secrets of the Poneglyphs. Once she accomplished&nbsp;
her dream of uncovering the true history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:58.200
what would she do? Well, she’d take the&nbsp;
secrets about the Ancient Weapons and use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:04.920
them to destroy the World Government. If they&nbsp;
thought the Buster Call on Ohara was justified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:11.360
just wait and see what destruction she could&nbsp;
cause with the Ancient Weapons at her disposal.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:19.040
When CP9 steals Robin away, the crew wouldn’t&nbsp;
save her because she’s their treasured friend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.360
They would do it because she’s their key&nbsp;
to reaching the end of the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.280
sought after by every major&nbsp;
pirate crew and the marines alike.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.120
While it’s tragic that Robin would spend&nbsp;
the rest of her life quietly suffering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:42.000
the bright side for us is that she’d keep the&nbsp;
cowboy hat and Uma Thurman bangs for way longer.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:51.000
Our next character wouldn’t be quietly&nbsp;
suffering. He’d actually be very loudly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:57.400
suffering. He’d turn his suffering up to&nbsp;
11, because making noise is his whole deal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:02.600
Brook’s entire crew died horrible deaths&nbsp;
while their ship was trapped inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:07.400
Florian Triangle. Thanks to his devil&nbsp;
fruit, he then found himself inhabiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:13.200
his own decayed skeleton. He was no longer flesh&nbsp;
and blood. He was a shadow of his former self,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:22.040
and then even that was stolen from him by&nbsp;
Gecko Moria. That’s enough to drive anyone mad.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:27.680
When the Evil Straw Hats™ would find themselves&nbsp;
in the shrouded mists of the Florian Triangle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.760
they’d encounter this skeleton&nbsp;
and immediately demand that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:37.880
join their. Just like Luffy immediately took&nbsp;
a liking to Brook, he would immediately want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:42.560
a cool skeleton on his crew. His face&nbsp;
perfectly matches their Jolly Roger.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:49.320
Brook’s dream is to eventually reunite with&nbsp;
Laboon. But having gone completely insane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:56.080
Evil Brook will only want to do so because&nbsp;
he’s pulled a complete Captain Ahab (except&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.720
instead of losing his leg, he’s lost all of&nbsp;
his skin). In his mind, twisted by loneliness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:06.360
he would think that Laboon had abandoned&nbsp;
him - his last friend alive leaving him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.120
to suffer in the Florian Triangle. With&nbsp;
his new signature weapon, The Guitarpoon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.600
in hand - he would take out Laboon and&nbsp;
then sell his blubber for huge profits.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:21.320
In this timeline, Bink’s Sake wouldn’t&nbsp;
just be a song for fun parties. For the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:25.000
Straw Hats’ enemies…it would&nbsp;
be the last thing they ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:32.160
hear. Brook isn’t the only Straw Hat&nbsp;
that would cease to be alive, either.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:39.560
In Franky’s dark timeline, as drawn by Oda, he&nbsp;
goes beyond being a cyborg who’s augmented his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:45.600
body into making himself fully a machine. Just&nbsp;
like Dr. Vegapunk did to Kuma, Franky would use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:52.880
his mechanical know-how to turn himself into the&nbsp;
ultimate weapon: The Battle Franky 50. In Oda’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:59.960
dark timeline drawing, he looks like his main body&nbsp;
has just become the General Franky - and he says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:06.560
the foreboding line that he must eliminate all&nbsp;
ships. This would make him the perfect addition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:12.280
to the Straw Hats’ crew - as they traveled across&nbsp;
the Grand Line, he would sink the ships of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:18.360
rival warlords, supernovas, and emperors&nbsp;
alike in his mission to destroy all ships.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:24.240
When the Straw Hats originally met Franky, he&nbsp;
was a crime lord in Water 7 leading his own gang.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:32.360
Instead of having a redemptive arc when he meets&nbsp;
the Straw Hats, when he meets the #Evil Straw Hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:38.920
he would just fit right in just as he was. But&nbsp;
eventually, he’d do something even better than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:44.760
building the Straw Hats the Thousand Sunny. Oda&nbsp;
gives us another version of Franky 20 more years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:52.160
down the line where he’s turned himself into not&nbsp;
just a cyborg - but into the ultimate battleship:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.160 --> 00:11:00.880
The Battle Franky 70. He wouldn’t just build a&nbsp;
ship worthy of the Pirate King - he’d BE the ship.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:06.600
And this evil version of Franky would&nbsp;
have no reservations against utilizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:12.560
the Pluton blueprints that had been passed&nbsp;
down to him. It’s like that Battleship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:18.360
Franky would have the destructive power&nbsp;
of an Ancient Weapon built into him. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:23.360
since the Evil Straw Hat crew would then&nbsp;
essentially be using Pluton as their ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:33.960
they would be able to lay waste to anyone in&nbsp;
their path as they sailed to find the One Piece.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:41.880
Of course, to sail the Battleship Franky through&nbsp;
the Grand Line, this crew will need a navigator:

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:51.000
Cat Burglar Nami is already motivated by greed&nbsp;
- she craves riches and treasure like the pirate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:57.600
she is. And since she had years of experience on&nbsp;
the crew of the infamous Arlong, she’ll still fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:03.320
right in on the Evil Straw Hat crew. Once Luffy&nbsp;
gave Arlong a beating, Nami would know that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:09.080
she really wanted to make bank - for her own&nbsp;
gain, not to buy back Cocoyashi, then betting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:15.440
on Luffy would be the right move. After all, with&nbsp;
monsters like Luffy, Zoro, and Sanji on the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:21.600
all she’d have to do is lay back and steer&nbsp;
the ship while the treasure came flowing in.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:27.520
In this version of the Straw Hats, Nami would be&nbsp;
true to her name. Even though she’s called the Cat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:33.320
Burglar in her Wanted Posters, she’s rarely used&nbsp;
her skills of stealth and infiltration. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:39.880
other Straw Hats like Robin and Brook have&nbsp;
taken the stealth missions instead. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.360
Nami, however, wouldn’t just be in charge&nbsp;
of getting the Straw Hats to their next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.960
destination. She’d be robbing those&nbsp;
destinations blind and then going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:55.080
shopping sprees to fill every spare room of&nbsp;
the Battleship Franky with lavish luxuries.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:13:01.120
But what about Nami’s love of navigation and&nbsp;
map-making? Well, she learned something from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:07.640
her evil mentor Arlong. It’s a whole lot easier&nbsp;
to have someone else do the work for you. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:12.800
could use those riches she stole to simply pay&nbsp;
someone to make maps for her. Or better yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:18.080
she can just chain them up and force them&nbsp;
to do the work. Meanwhile, she can just sit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:23.960
back and relax while eating only the decadent&nbsp;
dishes prepared by her personal chef: Sanji

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:31.400
Oda’s drawings for a dark timeline&nbsp;
Sanji are fascinating. In the first one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:37.560
he stops caring about how gourmet his dishes&nbsp;
are - instead, he thinks all food is the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:43.080
as long as it fills your belly. Even though&nbsp;
this is a huge shift from his current mindset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:49.840
we feel he’d still pull out all the culinary&nbsp;
stops for Nami because his love for every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:58.880
beautiful woman isn’t going to change in even&nbsp;
the darkest alternate universe. Once he finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.600
found the All Blue, Sanji wouldn’t use it to&nbsp;
create the ultimate seafood dishes - instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:08.680
he’d start a commercial fishery, destroying&nbsp;
the All Blue’s ecosystem and using the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:14.320
funds to support his Evil Empire - because&nbsp;
Evil Sanji has a whole Kingdom to inherit.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:23.400
Oda also drew an even older version of Sanji that&nbsp;
has more terrifying implications. In a timeline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:31.040
where everything goes wrong, Sanji doesn’t&nbsp;
deny his Vinsmoke name, he embraces it. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:37.400
picture has Sanji looking exactly like his father,&nbsp;
Vinsmoke Judge. He’s grown out his mustache, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:43.920
will now be perfect for twirling villainously. As&nbsp;
a member of the Evil Straw Hats, he’d overtake his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:49.960
family for control of the Germa Kingdom. The&nbsp;
only thing scarier than seeing the Battleship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:58.400
Franky coming toward you…would be the Battleship&nbsp;
Franky followed by hundreds of giant Germa snails.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:07.080
And leading that massive fleet (including at&nbsp;
least 8000 men) under the Straw Hat banner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:13.480
would be Captain Sniper God King Usopp,&nbsp;
the master manipulator. Usopp’s greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:19.440
strength - other than his wicked aim - has always&nbsp;
been his ability as a liar. In the main story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:25.840
he uses this ability in heartwarming ways,&nbsp;
like cheering up Kaya with his stories. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:31.200
the dark timeline, Usopp would use this&nbsp;
ability to bend others to his will and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.640
trick them into doing his bidding: think a&nbsp;
long-nosed version of Johan from Monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:41.120
who could get innocent people to commit&nbsp;
murder with just a short conversation.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:45.200
With each of those Germa Snails&nbsp;
containing a battalion of giants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:51.600
the Evil Straw Hat Grand Fleet of Evil will be&nbsp;
sure to strike fear into every island across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:57.880
the five seas of One Piece. And as for Usopp:&nbsp;
Master of Lies, children everywhere will fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:02.960
him. Parents will tell their kids that they&nbsp;
had better behave because the Devilish Sniper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:09.680
King can hit a naughty person from anywhere in&nbsp;
the world. The only true words out of Usopp’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:14.680
mouth from this point on will be tales&nbsp;
of conquest, pillaging, and bloodlust.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:23.280
But that bloodlust pales in comparison to the&nbsp;
next Straw Hat: Roronoa Zoro. Zoro is already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:31.800
a savage swordsman with a secret heart of gold.&nbsp;
Take away that heart of gold and what do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:38.280
get? A true demon for the fighter and honorary&nbsp;
first mate of the Evil Straw Hats. For somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:43.320
whose epithets range from “Pirate Hunter”&nbsp;
and just straight up the “King of Hell”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:49.560
he might just belong on the Evil Straw Hat&nbsp;
Crew ™ more than the normal Straw Hats.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:55.360
Zoro never got to defeat his rival Kuina. Instead,&nbsp;
fate took his opportunity to become the strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.360 --> 00:17:00.640
away when Kuina died. In another timeline,&nbsp;
instead of taking her death with honor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:07.760
trying to achieve their shared dream for her sake,&nbsp;
Zoro would be consumed by rage. He would still try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:12.800
to become the greatest swordsman, but instead&nbsp;
of honoring the tenets of the Bushido Code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:20.080
he would mercilessly cut down anyone in his&nbsp;
path on his quest to become the strongest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:27.880
And that will be perfect for his role as the&nbsp;
right hand man of the Evil Straw Hat Luffy.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:37.520
Luffy grew up in terrible poverty. He saw&nbsp;
the difference between the Nobles and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:43.840
people who lived within the literal trash of the&nbsp;
Gray Terminal in his home in the Goa Kingdom. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:49.720
was abandoned by his own father. Shanks refused&nbsp;
to take him along as a pirate - in fact, if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:57.680
wasn’t for Shanks’ sacrifice of his arm, it’s very&nbsp;
easy to see how Luffy could have ended up much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:04.080
much different. He dealt with so much unfairness&nbsp;
and injustice. Before Shanks’ influence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:08.240
he thought that pirates should fight&nbsp;
back against the slightest grievance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:11.080
like when the Mountain Bandit&nbsp;
struck Shanks with a bottle.

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:17.120
What if Luffy was never taught that his tendency&nbsp;
for violence was wrong? That he should only fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:22.160
for things that are important, like to defend&nbsp;
the people he cares about? What if Luffy took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:27.840
all of the injustice he faced in his childhood&nbsp;
and decided that he should just turn the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:34.000
upside down…I mean, he’s already an absolute&nbsp;
force of nature - causing absolute chaos for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.760
the status quo on any island he travels to.&nbsp;
But this time, instead of the World Government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:44.520
thinking he’s evil while in reality, he’s beloved&nbsp;
by the people of the world - in this timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:51.040
he’d strike fear into their hearts&nbsp;
just like Eustass Kid or Blackbeard.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:59.600
Evil Luffy would probably look a lot like&nbsp;
Blackbeard, in fact - or act like him at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:05.840
after all, Luffy drinks enough milk to keep&nbsp;
all his teeth. These two members of the Worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:12.920
Generation are pretty much two sides of the same&nbsp;
coin as it is. Just like Blackbeard, Luffy would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:18.080
stop at nothing to achieve his dream of becoming&nbsp;
the Pirate King even if it means stomping all over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:24.160
the dreams of other people. The way it is now,&nbsp;
Luffy lifts people up wherever he goes - this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:30.120
Luffy would bring them down just like Blackbeard.&nbsp;
If Luffy was evil, he’d sell out anyone he needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:34.960
to: even if it was his own brother. In this&nbsp;
timeline, instead of Blackbeard turning in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:39.960
Ace to become a Warlord, Luffy would be willing&nbsp;
to turn in his own brother to the marines if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:46.320
means climbing the ladder of the pirate world.
After all, Luffy is no hero - a hero is someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:52.960
who shares his meat. But as captain of the&nbsp;
Evil Straw Hats, he’d be a straight up villain.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:20:00.880
Of course, if Luffy really was evil,&nbsp;
it’s unlikely his crew would ever join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:04.640
him in the first place. More likely,&nbsp;
if Luffy had a sudden change of heart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.880
it would be up to the Straw Hats to stop&nbsp;
him from causing some serious harm to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:17.000
world. It just makes you wonder: is Gear 5&nbsp;
Luffy so broken that the other Straw Hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:23.560
wouldn’t even stand a chance against him even&nbsp;
with their combined strength? Or would they be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:32.000
able to stop Luffy’s maniacal rampage? You’ll&nbsp;
just have to see how that battle shakes out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:38.360
in this video where I talk about what would&nbsp;
happen if Luffy fought all of the Straw Hats.

